                                        <h6 class="mb-3">

NISM Series XII: Securities Markets Foundation Mock Test and NISM Series XII Question Bank details

</h6><br><p>The NISM-Series-XII: Securities Markets Foundation Certification Examination is designed for individuals at the entry level who aspire to build a career in the securities markets. It is also beneficial for anyone seeking a fundamental understanding of the Indian Securities markets, including:</p>
										
                                        
                                        
                                       
                                       
                                        <div class="mb-4">
                                            <ul class="car-single-list">
                                                <li><i class="far fa-check-circle"></i>Entry-level professionals in the securities markets</li>
                                                <li><i class="far fa-check-circle"></i> Employees of intermediaries operating in the securities industry</li>
                                                <li><i class="far fa-check-circle"></i>Professionals from various industries interested in acquiring knowledge of the securities markets</li>
												 <li><i class="far fa-check-circle"></i>Students</li>
												 <li><i class="far fa-check-circle"></i>Homemakers</li>
												 <li><i class="far fa-check-circle"></i>Teachers</li>
                                               
                                            </ul>
											<br><p>This voluntary examination aims to provide participants with basic knowledge of the Indian securities markets and the associated rules and regulations.</p>
                                        </div>
										<h6 class="mb-3">Examination Objectives</h6>
										<p>Upon successful completion of the examination, candidates should:</p>
										 <ul class="car-single-list">
                                                <li><i class="far fa-check-circle"></i>Possess a foundational understanding of the basics of the Indian Securities Markets.</li>
                                                <li><i class="far fa-check-circle"></i>Demonstrate knowledge of the various processes involved in Primary and Secondary Markets.</li>
                                                <li><i class="far fa-check-circle"></i>Exhibit comprehension of the schemes and products in Mutual Funds and Derivatives Markets in India.</li>
                                               
                                            </ul>
										<h6 class="mb-3">Assessment Structure</h6>
                                        

<p>

The exam comprises 100 questions, each carrying 1 mark, and candidates are allotted 2 hours for completion. To pass the examination, candidates need to achieve a minimum score of 60%. Importantly, there is no negative marking applied for incorrect answers.
</p>

